## Why This Is Asked

This asks for a practical, beginner-friendly AWS AI/ML workflow that combines text detection, translation, sentiment, storage, and a lightweight read API, while emphasizing security and cost.

## Key Concepts

- DetectDominantLanguage (Comprehend)
- TranslateText (Translate)
- DetectSentiment (Comprehend)
- S3 → Lambda → Step Functions orchestration
- DynamoDB indexing by documentId
- API Gateway + Lambda for reads
- IAM least privilege and KMS
- Privacy: PII masking, encryption, and retention

## Code Example

```javascript
import { ComprehendClient, DetectDominantLanguageCommand, DetectSentimentCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-comprehend";
import { TranslateClient, TranslateTextCommand } from "@aws-sdk/client-translate";

const comprehend = new ComprehendClient({region:"us-east-1"});
const translate = new TranslateClient({region:"us-east-1"});

async function analyzeText(text){
  const dl = await comprehend.send(new DetectDominantLanguageCommand({Text: text}));
  const langCode = (dl.Languages?.[0]?.LanguageCode) ?? "en";
  let english = text;
  if (langCode !== "en"){
    const tr = await translate.send(new TranslateTextCommand({Text: text, SourceLanguageCode: langCode, TargetLanguageCode: "en"}));
    english = tr.TranslatedText;
  }
  const sentiment = await comprehend.send(new DetectSentimentCommand({Text: english, LanguageCode: "en"}));
  return { language: langCode, translated: english, sentiment: sentiment.Sentiment };
}
``` 

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this with mocks and local development?
- What are the implications for cost at scale and how would you mitigate?
- How would you handle a batch of emails arriving concurrently?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical ability to design an end-to-end, event-driven image analytics pipeline in AWS using beginner-friendly services (S3, Lambda, Rekognition, DynamoDB) with real-world concerns like privacy, cost, and tenancy.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven flow triggered by S3 PUT
- Rekognition detectLabels with top N labels
- Lightweight color palette extraction in Lambda
- Descriptor JSON stored in S3 and DynamoDB upsert
- IAM least privilege, DLQ/backoff, cost awareness

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js Lambda pseudo
const rek = new AWS.Rekognition();
const s3 = new AWS.S3();
const ddb = new AWS.DynamoDB.DocumentClient();

exports.handler = async (evt) => {
  const key = evt.Records[0].s3.object.key;
  const bucket = evt.Records[0].s3.bucket.name;
  const img = await s3.getObject({Bucket:bucket,Key:key}).promise();
  const labels = await rek.detectLabels({Image:{Bytes: img.Body}, MaxLabels:3, MinConfidence: 60}).promise();
  const colors = extractColors(img.Body); // simple utility
  const descriptor = { imageKey:key, labels: labels.Labels.map(l=>l.Name), colors, timestamp: Date.now(), facesDetected: labels.Labels.some(l=>l.Name==='Face') };
  await s3.putObject({Bucket: bucket, Key: key + '.json', Body: JSON.stringify(descriptor)}).promise();
  await ddb.update({TableName:'ProductImages',Key:{productId: determineProductId(key)}, UpdateExpression:'SET labels=:l, colors=:c, imageKey=:k, privacyFlag=:p', ExpressionAttributeValues:{':l':descriptor.labels, ':c':descriptor.colors, ':k':key, ':p':false}}).promise();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate labels and handle false positives? 
- How would you extend for multi-tenant isolation and cost controls?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to build a scalable, privacy-preserving ML pipeline that composes multiple AWS services (S3, Step Functions, Lambda, SageMaker) with governance and observability.

## Key Concepts

- Event-driven pipelines with S3 triggers
- Step Functions coordinating Lambda and SageMaker
- PII redaction in Lambda
- SageMaker inference integration for sentiment and topics
- Data governance: KMS encryption, least-privilege IAM, auditing
- Reliability: DLQ, retries, monitoring, cost controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Lambda pseudocode for redacting PII from JSON input
exports.handler = async (event) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(event.body || '{}');
  if (data.email) data.email = '[REDACTED]';
  if (data.phone) data.phone = '[REDACTED]';
  return { redacted: true, data };
};
```

